<title>POLAND: PBR revises down 1996 earnings.</title>
<headline>PBR revises down 1996 earnings.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>PBR SA results for the financial year ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of zlotys unless stated)</p>
<p>JANUARY-DECEMBER</p>
<p>    operating profit		     45.17   vs  35.58</p>
<p>    pre-tax profit			 45.19   vs  35.68</p>
<p>    net profit			     20.39   vs  14.00</p>
<p>    revenues from securities	    0.16   vs   0.04</p>
<p>    interest and similar revenues   188.34   vs 159.45</p>
<p>    interest and similar costs	124.20   vs  94.07</p>
<p>    revenues from commission	   11.39   vs  11.28</p>
<p>    costs of commission		   3.22   vs   2.91</p>
<p>    income tax			     24.80   vs  21.68</p>
<p>    other taxes			     0.00   vs   0.00</p>
<p>    extraordinary			   0.02   vs   0.10</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name is Polski Bank Rozwoju SA. In its quarterly results PBR reported a net of 28.26 million. It also showed revised up income tax from earlier reported 19.50</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
